# 4. Mutation run: each of 143 deliberate changes applied alone to a scratch copy of the bundle. Script: outputs/mutate-gitlab-m1.sh   Output: outputs/mutation-run.txt
$ TMPDIR=<scratch> TERRAFORM=<terraform binary> PYLIB=<PyYAML directory> bash outputs/mutate-gitlab-m1.sh <worktree>
Baseline 26 of 26 pass on the unmutated tree. Mutations 143: caught 143, not caught 0. A change counts as caught only when the changed file still parses
(bash -n; PyYAML safe_load; terraform fmt's parser, exit 2 on a syntax error), differs from the original, and the test fails on a named case. Three
changes are meant to break the syntax (case 14); the harness requires that they do.
History: the first run of the first 138 changes against the first version of the test left 6 survivors (the GitHub token written to a file, the GitHub token
logged, the backup archive not uploaded, the configuration archive not uploaded, the configuration archive without /etc/gitlab, the backup script not
stopping on error). The test was tightened for those (cases 17 and 21), case 3 was rewritten, and the test now reads files when a case runs. After the reviewer's
first round (the lane file, review of 09:30Z) case 8 was tightened (no `*` in any action or resource string, policies only as data documents) with 5 new changes
that exercise it, and the exact-text pins of the secret-name alignment and the two token prompts were relaxed; the recorded run is the last one.

